+# PRD derivation review
+
+- reviewer: Codex
+- reviewed_at: 2026-10-10
+- source: exact approved UR.md
+- destination: unapproved PRD.md
+- assurance: cooperative semantic mapping; not independent human review, approval or QA
+- result: ready for canonical recording and human product decision
+
+| Approved UR signal | PRD criteria | Meaning retained |
+|---|---|---|
+| AC-001 | AC-001, AC-008 | Same current state; complete UX/source state; historical effect versus fresh observation |
+| AC-002 | AC-002 | Stable semantic routing, no prose policy |
+| AC-003 | AC-003 | Supported forms/diagnostics shared with executing owners |
+| AC-004 | AC-004, AC-005, AC-006 | Existing recording/presentation/approval/revision owners and exact human decisions |
+| AC-005 | AC-007, AC-008 | Qualified per-write retry/conflict/concurrency/uncertainty/recovery |
+| AC-006 | AC-009 | Structured closeout plus Quick Task compatibility; no repeated OR or Git effect |
+| AC-007 | AC-010, AC-011, AC-015 | Current versus historical evidence; exact documents/draft checks; scoped locale regression |
+| AC-008 | AC-012, AC-013 | Actual transport parity, compatible contracts and honest candidate/host assurance |
+| AC-009 | AC-014 | One common design and whole-chain acceptance; measured reduction of routine discovery/manual edits |
+
+The ready UX analysis supplies working-mode/effective-state/actor/blocker/recovery definitions. Brownfield supplies full-depth ownership/compatibility risks. Neither replaces the approved UR. Existing revision constraints remain supported-only; no new runtime-authority or app-write feature was inferred. Current evidence can remain unknown when exact association is absent. The zero routine discovery/manual-edit target operationalizes the UR's supported-flow goal and leaves normal engineering reviews intact.
+
+Before-PRD rows propose scope/authority/evidence/acceptance already derived from the approved need. Later-SD rows concern exact technical ownership, formats, API grouping, compatibility and recovery; later-TP concerns executable qualification. No undecided material user need is silently deferred. These rows remain subject to the new PRD decision, not a claimed human approval.
+
+Authoring-readiness MCP returned ready=true at revision c54989b5-7be9-4a85-a5fb-e651540fc3a2 with PRD digest sha256:579386038f52a54fd23d2a253e4927bbde755380e638493614e7ae69539a9097. This covers authoring checks only. The writer must still validate exact source mapping, registration and current revision; a fresh presentation and deliberate response remain required.
