+
+## Derivation
+
+| Approved UR signal | PRD criteria | Reasoned coverage |
+|---|---|---|
+| AC-001 | AC-001, AC-008 | Shared current state and historical effect remain separate; renewed UX and no-revision flows included. |
+| AC-002 | AC-002 | Canonical typed continuation is independent of equivalent display wording. |
+| AC-003 | AC-003 | Supported authoring forms, executing-version guidance and concrete diagnostics agree. |
+| AC-004 | AC-004, AC-005, AC-006, AC-017 | Actual ordered recording, exact presentation, same decision authority and supported revision are bound; review evidence cannot manufacture QA/approval. |
+| AC-005 | AC-007, AC-008, AC-019 | Each writer retains operation-specific uncertainty/retry/conflict/recovery; click/text adds explicit at-most-one effective gate decision. |
+| AC-006 | AC-009 | Both structured modes and Quick Task closeout distinguish missing obligations, pending synchronization and completed governance; no Git side effect. |
+| AC-007 | AC-010, AC-011, AC-015 | Current/unknown/history evidence, exact readable versions, draft checks, foreign data and localization remain protected. |
+| AC-008 | AC-012, AC-013 | Actual transport parity, explicit compatibility and identity-bound evidence; no native or stronger provenance claim from mere tool access. |
+| AC-009 | AC-014 | Common design and whole-chain acceptance with fixed before/after corpus; searches/manual steps measured separately from necessary user decisions and normal engineering. |
+| AC-010 | AC-016, AC-017 | Concise complete current card, meaningful comparison or unavailable comparison, exact larger document, return/discussion, three actions and later still-current exact text. |
+| AC-011 | AC-018, AC-019 | Human intent, host permission and canonical effect are distinct; no second business decision for permission, no duplicate effect, no invented independent human proof. |
