+## Semantic review
+
+The design preserves the approved supported lifecycle rather than adding unrelated diagnostics or generic function access. One command selector delegates to current operation-specific owners. Readers, schemas and projections do not become gate permission authorities. Each of the 15 PRD criteria is mapped exactly once in SD; all 14 SDD decisions are used. Reviewed responses and their practical boundaries:
+
+| Approved criterion | Derivation assessment |
+|---|---|
+| AC-001 | Complete state preparation includes UX and source-revision context in proposed and persisted states. Fresh post-write observation prevents cached pre-state from masquerading as current state. |
+| AC-002 | Semantic operation/actor replaces executable sentence comparison. Descriptive instructions remain usable without becoming permission. |
+| AC-003 | Existing parsing/readiness owns shared supported grammar and diagnostics; selected metadata includes bindings without fabricating reviewed mappings. Accepted legacy forms are preserved. |
+| AC-004 | Existing internal/artefact writers accept actual results in eligible order and record relationship/receipt coherently. Report registration copies the actual decision; no QA or human judgement is invented. |
+| AC-005 | Presentation and deliberate response are distinct commands with exact bindings and cooperative assurance. Historical replay includes fresh current observation rather than old permission. |
+| AC-006 | Existing early PRD and late CD+Tests boundaries remain; exact historical bytes and supported preview/apply/recovery are required. No universal source revision is introduced. |
+| AC-007 | Family-specific UUID/request digests, existing locks, strict owned journal stages and explicit effect uncertainty address replay, payload conflict, concurrent change and lost responses. Unknown interference blocks. |
+| AC-008 | Receipt effect and current availability/revision remain separate, including stale receipt or current-read failure. |
+| AC-009 | Structured OR-full uses existing applicable quality, approval and context requirements. Journal-based OR/Run/backlog consistency and corrected completion semantics preserve Quick Task and exclude automatic VCS. |
+| AC-010 | Current, superseded and unknown applicability derive from real bindings. New associations do not invent legacy history or retrospectively change decisions. |
+| AC-011 | Existing read-only cockpit projections, document proof, snapshot/generation guards and session state remain owners. No new app command or approval access is introduced. |
+| AC-012 | Shared Core descriptors/validation feed CLI/MCP; new qualified writers and dual readers preserve receipt and read compatibility. Older executing policy is explicitly outside new qualification. Transport disablement does not roll back persisted effects. |
+| AC-013 | Exact generated candidate, actual MCP, affected Codex interaction/teardown and locale evidence are separate obligations. No automatic installation, host equivalence or stronger human provenance is claimed. |
+| AC-014 | Dependent stages and retained before/after corpus measure routine discovery/manual editing while preserving decisions and negative checks. Necessary engineering investigation is not falsely counted as a product defect. |
+| AC-015 | Protected source/foreign Run hashes, exact document semantics and rendered registered locales are retained as required regression evidence. |
+
+The PRD's later-SD questions are concretely answered: complete state preparation and semantic continuation, bounded tool grouping/generated schemas, qualified legacy convergence and dual readers, operation-specific retry/locking/recovery, multi-record closeout, shared authoring interpretation and evidence applicability. Later-TP rows defer executable tasks/scenario IDs and observations only; no binding architecture or product need is hidden there.
+
+Existing owner reuse is supported by read-only source inspection of the state reader/policy, Core service boundary, CLI/MCP worker, artefact and approval writers, early/late revision, Run/backlog transaction and authoring/cockpit owners. SDD-007's strict journal v3, new receipts, selected metadata and structured closeout are proposed extensions, not claims of existing implementation. Scope remains substantial but coherent: all dependent stages must pass whole-flow acceptance. Schema budget, old-writer behavior and multi-file recovery are explicit risks with tests, not accepted debt or presumed atomicity.
+
+The early revision history extension preserves the existing eligibility boundary. The recovery selector excludes generic seal repair and foreign pending operations. Conservative aggregate tool annotations do not make per-action replay guarantees. Distinct installed runtime digests are not treated as package equivalence. Any preparation evidence contradicting these decisions returns to the appropriate SD/source revision owner before implementation.
+
+## Readiness and recording
+
+Bound MCP artifact-readiness at revision 8a5b473f-7aee-472b-835c-5f2a91494c87 reported authoring ready: localized summary, sd-decisions-v1 and criteria-chain-v1 passed with no diagnostics. This is structural evidence, distinct from this semantic assessment. Canonical source mapping and reviewed registration must still succeed before presentation. New deliberate Approval: SD is required; prior PRD approval grants no implementation permission.
+
+Review outcome: suitable for canonical draft registration and a new SD decision, subject to unchanged exact approved source and current revision. No implementation, QA, release or independent human-review result is asserted.
