+# TP derivation review
+
+Date: 2026-10-10
+Reviewer: Codex
+Run: core-mcp-flow-coherence-20261010-01
+Expected authoring revision: 663a80a9-26e3-474a-b3dc-e4056ef64e23
+Approved source: SD.md, sha256:6cef01ba44934f991f3e6701e9d386fe084f6c8a3386e5e6d3d060b2c606a619; approved through presentation 27fc175a-567f-4e80-90e6-728b2523e374.
+Approved product input: PRD.md, sha256:4d876d26b7bcc207bf2b6067ca5d5a1c0acf81999949044c41eedefca1cce2db.
+Reviewed destination: TP.md, sha256:696823b836b074243a48f90fe2a4a6dbbfea61682ad86fdbf6a919fdc7354b91.
+Assurance: cooperative semantic derivation review, not independent human review, implementation or QA evidence.
+
+## Assessment
+
+The plan uses the supplied approved PRD/SD as product/design authorities. Twelve dependent tasks implement their shared-owner architecture in one Run: actual preparation/baseline, complete state and semantic routing, shared contracts/grammar, writer/evidence/transaction extensions, exact decisions/deduplication, supported revisions, closeout/current evidence, CLI/MCP, focused card, generated transport/locale qualification, actual native human observation, and required reviews/QA aggregation. No task starts implementation before TP approval and fulfilled Brownfield preparation. No independent fixes, automatic installation/restart, Git action or new product gate is introduced.
+
+Forty-five stable scenarios cover all 21 criteria and all 18 design decisions, including every criterion-to-SD-decision association. The table uses exactly one decision identity per criterion/scenario row; repeated evidence is reused without duplicate scenario effect. Every scenario names a declared task, concrete stimulus, observable expected result and specific run-local future evidence output. Evidence paths and expected results are clearly planned, not falsely passing reports. Task dependencies follow approved ownership and contain no cycle.
+
+Failure coverage follows the actual boundary: same-state/full-versus-short writer discrepancy; prose-insensitive routing; format/schema/budget/unsafe path rejection; exact current presentation/human response; wrong-order/actual revise recording; per-write UUID/payload/global collision/replay; archive/owned-output/Run/backlog interruption and old journal recovery; known historical receipt versus unavailable current reader; early UR-at-SD and retained existing revision policy; current/history/unknown evidence; OR/quality/context completion; disabled/cross-group permissions; dispatched worker uncertainty; card/version/comment/rejection guard and text/click conflict; session expiry before/after dispatch and stale-result retirement.
+
+The exact native Codex sequence uses genuine human test actions on disposable versions and separately captured canonical receipts. Reading/discussion does not decide, host consent is not a second business decision, and app-only/session metadata does not become independent human-origin proof. Native permission/accessibility/all-language/teardown gaps remain missing evidence; source/browser/text-only tests cannot substitute. Earlier user observations and the bootstrap retain their own identities; the actual same-Run revision archive is read-only evidence and is requalified rather than mutated again.
+
+Before/after comparisons retain conditions, protected reference hashes and negative checks; engineering source inspection and legitimate user/external actions are counted separately. No weaker-model claim is implied by deterministic success. Existing review owners and qa-gate retain their actual responsibilities. Architectural/authority/budget contradiction returns to the approved design/source owner before work, rather than allowing an improvised adapter or debt exception.
+
+## Readiness and proof limits
+
+Fresh actual MCP artifact-readiness reports ready=true at the expected authoring revision and exact destination digest, with complete German summary and criteria-chain-v1 pass, no diagnostics. Earlier checks found missing criterion/design associations and duplicate/single-decision mapping format; corrected through the bound unregistered TP using MCP diagnostics, with no parser-source inspection, validator change or relaxed check. Semantic assessment here complements but does not replace machine readiness.
+
+This review supports initial TP-derived_from-SD registration with update_draft=false, fresh mapping/input paths and a new bound TP presentation. Only a deliberate Approval: TP allows actual implementation preparation; this review grants no code, QA, UAT or release authority.
+
+Post-registration: the existing reviewed artefact writer recorded TP-derived_from-SD, update_draft=false, using TP_MAPPING_01.json and TP_RECORDING_01.json at revision 20 / f91f1c0f-0658-4901-9b49-b1e222c0af1a; backlog updated. Fresh bound MCP gate-check reports doctor pass, no blocker and presentation_required for TP. Canonical digests of approved UR/PRD/SD and registered Brownfield/UX were verified unchanged before registration; git diff --check passed. These observations qualify authoring/recording only, not implementation, native acceptance or QA.
