+# MCP candidate observations — deliberate user decision interaction
+
+These observations continue the user's additional assignment. They do not create API authority or implementation permission.
+
+| Activity | Observation | Assessment / existing owner |
+|---|---|---|
+| Approved-source change routing | prd_action revise against a Run with approved UR/PRD and linked SD returned a terminal SD status card without explaining an available revision path | Clear capability/unsupported-lifecycle orientation remains a metadata/diagnostic candidate; do not patch protected sources or invent a reopen. Existing revision/control owner must expose the limitation. |
+| Core/MCP scope comparison | Referenced URs were read to distinguish current lifecycle scope, explanatory cards and the broader maturity roadmap | Required semantic scope matching is normal evidence work; titles/recency/blank UR do not establish a match. No generic code-search API follows. |
+| New Run bookkeeping | Canonical run-create succeeded and returned documented plain text containing revision_id; an attempted JSON parse failed after the successful effect | Caller parsing mistake; the command must not be retried as if creation failed. Typed output description can improve consuming guidance; no writer bypass or new authority. |
+| UR preparation | Bound continuation named a local UR template path that does not exist; explicit runtime sections/language and established UR format remained available | Concrete authoring-resource guidance candidate, not permission to install/repair runtime or substitute a validator. |
+| UR readiness | Existing bound artifact-readiness returned ready with exact digest and no diagnostics | Confirmed reuse of existing MCP function; no direct validator/source-signature search needed. |
+
+The native click-to-gate input is a new user-interaction boundary. Host tool consent and a model-created exact string do not prove a deliberate user action. Brownfield/SD must determine actual host support and retain honest assurance before implementation. No weaker-model benefit or native execution has been measured here.
