+# UR derivation review — user decision card
+
+Date: 2026-10-10
+Reviewer: Codex
+Assurance: cooperative content review, not gate approval, independent user provenance or native host qualification.
+
+The user accepted the proposed decision card with exact document access, three actions, discussion, progress/confirmed result and truthful replaced-version history, then instructed continuation. The latest clarification asks whether exact Approval text remains usable later during AI discussion. UR preserves both input routes as equal choices, subject to current presentation/eligibility. It explicitly excludes approval inferred from questions, quotations, examples, model payloads or remembered tool permission.
+
+The original core-mcp-flow-coherence UR was inspected: new app approval buttons are excluded. Approved PRD and registered SD already depend on it. The prior attempted prd_action revise returned a terminal SD status card without revision authorization. No approved source was edited or old response applied. Canonical intake inventory was consumed; referenced actionable-card and maturity-roadmap URs were inspected. They concern explanatory non-authorizing cards and broad coordination respectively, not this exact native-click slice. The incomplete approval-card-decision-focus candidate has no UR and supplies no confirmed scope. A new bounded complementary Run was therefore bound through the existing new/resume intake, with no transfer of approvals.
+
+All nine acceptance signals derive from accepted interaction requirements: readable decision, exact inspection, three actions, discussion/equal text route, actual human origin distinct from permission, fault/concurrency feedback, current/history state, existing-owner reuse and actual native/localized evidence. Technical actor-proof and host integration remain explicit design obligations; the UR does not pretend that a UI nonce/message or text generated by the agent proves independent human origin. A safe text fallback remains available but alone cannot qualify the new click feature.
+
+No new formal gate, general dashboard, automatic lifecycle/Git action or foreign Run edits are required. Existing presentation/approval/readiness/receipt/recovery and document/session owners are reused. Pending Core/MCP work creates sequencing/compatibility obligations to resolve before implementation, not a license to implement a second writer or approve its pending SD. A materially impossible host capability must remain an explicit blocker, not a synthetic test success.
+
+The supplied template path is absent locally; authoring used the explicit required sections/language fields in the bound ur-definition contract and existing approved UR format, without modifying templates or runtime. Bound MCP artifact-readiness at revision 153fe9e3-fa00-4bac-b29c-30e1a8e11c36 passed summary and ur_readiness with no diagnostics, digest sha256:67a506093d1c966e80bbeeab11b87d30153e21fb1fdd232649a1b4098d60a946. This is authoring evidence; canonical registration/presentation/new human approval remain necessary.
+
+Semantic outcome: user intent is sufficiently concrete for a new UR decision; no material product clarification remains. Architecture, host proof, exact task/evidence planning and actual implementation remain future governed work.
